-- title:
--   More Asymmetry released q=5 fourth-power parameters (exact rationals)
-- statement:
--   The released q = 5 fourth-power parameters of More Asymmetry, as exact rationals with common denominator 10^15 (integer numerators): the global-stage distribution over the 45 level-3 shapes and its max-entropy Lagrange multipliers for each of the six regions; for each of the 126 positive level-3 terms its global region, shape, six region proportions, admissible splits, split distribution per region and Lagrange multipliers; the complete split distributions of the 144 zero-coordinate level-3 terms; and the split parameter of each positive-mass level-2 112- or 022-type term. Recomputed exactly with the paper's stage formulas and Gibbs-dual penalty bounds, these data give log copies 2.8130209845673 and log matrix size 2.0961236751733 per fourth-power copy, a margin of 1.885e-6 over 4 ln 7 at tau = 3952233/5000000.
-- source:
--   Alman, Duan, Vassilevska Williams, Xu, Xu, Zhou, More Asymmetry Yields Faster Matrix Multiplication, arXiv:2404.16349v3, Section 7; released code and parameters at https://osf.io/mw5ak/?view_only=5769f03789354793b61e11aac4dd85dd (data/W1.00_2.371339.mat), rounded to rationals over 10^15.

import Mathlib.Data.Rat.Defs
import Mathlib.Tactic.DeriveFintype

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option maxRecDepth 100000

namespace MME.MoreAsymmetryReleased

/-! Released q = 5 fourth-power parameters of More Asymmetry (arXiv:2404.16349v3, Section 7;
code and data at osf.io/mw5ak, `data/W1.00_2.371339.mat`), rounded to rationals with common
denominator `den = 10^15` and repaired so that every probability vector sums to exactly one.
Entries are integer numerators; the rational value is `numerator / den`.  Level-3 shapes and splits
follow the authors' `PrepareShapes` / `PrepareSplits` order; regions follow `Dims` (lexicographic
permutations of X, Y, Z). -/

